The question asks whether a PHP interface can declare constants.

In PHP, interfaces can indeed declare constants. Interface constants are always public and cannot be modified. This is a feature that has been available since PHP 5.

Example:
```php
interface MyInterface {
    const MAX = 100;
    public function doSomething();
}
```

